From c4bf9b88ddcf0d42436ebfcfe157a56dca95897d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeanluca <jeanlucafp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:52:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tmserver): show the Kefra balance panel and answer it at
 the Sobrevivente

The Hall of Kefra balance (_DN_CHANGE_COUNT) went out through w.Send, which
stamps the session's conn in HEADER.ID. The 7662 client only shows a
MSG_MessagePanel with ID 0 (TMScene.cpp:1371), so players never saw how many
entries a sealed scroll gave or how many were left, and read it as "one
access" (#343). The text was also UTF-8 instead of the legacy Windows-1252.

- send the balance like SendClientMessage (ID 0, Language.txt bytes); the
  Nightmare balance and /nt share the string and get the same fix
- the Sobrevivente answers with the balance when the player has no scroll
  (intentional deviation from the silent legacy, asked by #343)
- entries per scroll configurable: -kefra-entries-per-scroll /
  W2PP_KEFRA_ENTRIES_PER_SCROLL, default 100 (legacy)

Closes #343

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
